Race Filters and Candidate Providers

Purpose
    Implement race filters as candidate-set providers instead of ranking criteria.
    Candidate flow: internal unit-scope provider -> active race-filter provider -> unit snapshots -> name filter and ranking criteria -> UI.
    Default unit scope: citizens-and-pets.
    Default race scope: include Humanoids.

Behavioral invariants
    ☐ Attribute, trait, and skill filters remain ordered ranking criteria with unchanged scoring and tie-break behavior.
    ☐ Race filters never contribute to matched count, score, weighted score, ranking priority, or the Stats matched-criteria table.
    ☐ Positive race filters form a union; negative race filters subtract from that union; exclusions win over inclusions.
    ☐ Active-unit ordering is preserved and no candidate unit is returned more than once.
    ☐ Every valid filter state contains at least one positive race filter; restore include Humanoids when necessary.
    ☐ Saved individual-race filters use stable creature IDs, never world raw-vector indices.
    ☐ Existing UI geometry, focus behavior, mouse hitboxes, result selection retention, zoom behavior, and ranking semantics remain intact.

