Phase 3 - Build the race catalog and compound predicates
    ✔ Add a dedicated race catalog module rather than embedding creature-raw policy in descriptors.lua or search.lua. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Generate individual descriptors with stable IDs in the form race:raw:<CREATURE_ID>. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Generate compound descriptors with IDs in the form race:group:<KEY>. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Define ordered compounds for Humanoids, Trainable Animals, Domestic Animals, Wild Animals, Megabeasts, and Vermin. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Derive compound membership from centralized creature/caste raw predicates and document the exact flags used by each group. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Handle missing world raws, creature IDs, names, castes, and flags without crashing or accidentally matching a unit. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Display compounds first in their defined order, then individual races alphabetically by display label with stable-ID tie-breaking. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Keep citizen, resident, visitor, and hostile classifications out of the race catalog; they belong to unit scope. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Reset raw-derived race metadata through the existing world/module lifecycle. @done(26-07-12)
    Phase gate
        ✔ Catalog tests cover stable IDs, labels, ordering, duplicate protection, missing raws, and every compound predicate. @done(26-07-12)
        ✔ Reordering the raw vector does not change a saved individual-race filter ID or its resolved creature. @done(26-07-12; 148 tests, 0 failures)

Phase 4 - Implement the active race-filter provider and state invariants
    ✔ Add a race candidate provider that wraps any SoulSearchCandidateProvider. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Resolve active race descriptors once per provider pass instead of once per unit. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Union all positive race matches. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Remove every negative race match after inclusion so exclusions always win. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Preserve upstream order and suppress duplicates when compounds and individual races overlap. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Make a new or first-loaded filter state default to include race:group:HUMANOIDS. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Prevent remove, clear, replace, preset load, or stale-ID validation from leaving state without a positive race scope; restore Humanoids. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Define Clear all as clearing ranking filters and resetting candidate filters to include Humanoids. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Ensure negative-only external/preset input is normalized by adding positive Humanoids before applying exclusions. @done(26-07-12)
    Phase gate
        ✔ Tests cover dwarves/elves/humans under Humanoids and dogs under animal groups. @done(26-07-12)
        ✔ Tests cover multiple-positive union, overlapping groups, exclusions, all humanoids except dwarves, and trainable animals except dogs. @done(26-07-12)
        ✔ Tests cover removal of the final positive, negative-only input, stale IDs, clear, replace, save/load, and preset load. @done(26-07-12; 154 tests, 0 failures)

Phase 5 - Move candidate acquisition ahead of snapshots and ranking
    ✔ Separate resident/unit snapshot construction from candidate collection in residents.lua. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Replace direct getCitizens() ownership with snapshot construction over units supplied by the provider chain. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Make snapshots safe for animals and other units without souls, skills, translated names, professions, traits, or mental attributes. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Preserve unit identity and live position access required by result selection and map zoom. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Change UI refresh orchestration to build the provider chain, obtain candidates, snapshot them, then invoke search.apply. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Pass only ranking filters to search.apply; do not add race branches to value evaluation, scoring, or result comparison. @done(26-07-12)
    ✔ Recompute candidates and results whenever active race filters change. @done(26-07-12)
    Phase gate
        ✔ Search tests prove race selection changes membership but never scoring or ordering among the surviving rows. @done(26-07-12)
        ✔ Existing ranking characterization tests remain green without race-specific conditions in search.lua. @done(26-07-12)
        ✔ Snapshot tests cover citizens, named pets, unnamed livestock, and units without souls. @done(26-07-12; 157 tests, 0 failures)

